-- title:
--   Rank-one torsor grading on a Hopf algebra block
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, an exponent $k$, and a finite abelian group $\Lambda$ with decidable equality such that $q^k g = 0$ for all $g \in \Lambda$. Let $L$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $0$, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, and let $O$ be a commutative domain equipped with an injective algebra map to $L$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $O$ is a discrete valuation ring in which the image of $q$ is irreducible. Let $HO$ be a commutative ring that is a Hopf algebra over $O$, module-finite and flat over $O$, with cocommutative comultiplication, let $p_0 \colon HO \to O[\Lambda]$ (the monoid algebra on $\Lambda$ written multiplicatively) be a surjective coalgebra-and-algebra map, and let $e \in HO$ be idempotent. Assume that exactly $\lvert\Lambda\rvert$ elements $\psi$ of `WithConv (HO →ₐ[O] L)`, the $O$-algebra homomorphisms $HO \to L$ carried by the convolution type synonym, satisfy $\psi(e) = 1$. For $j \in \Lambda$ write $L_j$ for the $O$-submodule of those $t \in HO$ with $(p_0 \otimes \mathrm{id})(\Delta t) = j \otimes t$, in the Finsupp form provided by [`HopfAlgebra.TorsorGrading.blockComponents`](def/HopfAlgebra_TorsorGrading.html#L55), and $te = t$. Then: $L_0 = Oe$; each $L_j$ is generated by a single element $t$; $L_{i+j}$ lies in the $O$-span of the products $xy$ with $x \in L_i$, $y \in L_j$; conversely $L_i L_j \subseteq L_{i+j}$; and every $x \in HO$ with $xe = x$ lies in $\bigsqcup_{j}$, i.e. the supremum $\bigvee_{j \in \Lambda} L_j$ of the submodules $L_j$.
--
--   This is the structural core of the Raynaud–Mazur analysis of a block of a finite flat cocommutative Hopf algebra over an absolutely unramified discrete valuation ring: the block $HOe$ decomposes as a $\Lambda$-graded algebra whose graded pieces are free of rank one, so that the block is a torsor under the group scheme dual to $O[\Lambda]$. It is used by [`KummerO.exists_units_of_block_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#KummerO.exists_units_of_block_of_isAlgClosed) to produce the unit generators entering the Kummer-theoretic description of such blocks.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_blockPieces_torsor_core_of_isAlgClosed.lean

